+# T2_F285 — Findings paydown v4
+**Tier 2 · Depends on: nothing new — every id below is a finding already registered in `.agent/live_review.md` · Blocks/used by: every later closure, whose integrity precondition reads the open set this feature pays down**
+
+> Registered 2026-09-24 by F284's closure, under operator amendment amend0911-feedback rule B
+> (the rolling findings paydown, one per five features), and placed directly after F026, the fifth
+> unaccepted STATUS line below the position F284 held (DECISION F284 D3).
+> REGISTERED THIN: nothing in this file has been implemented. Its first round reads the open set
+> and writes the slice list, one slice per module, from every open finding registered before the
+> claim date whose repair fits one round; the finding text is the spec.
+
+## Goal & Done
+Pay down the open findings that describe a real defect, each by the repair its own text names,
+with the evidence that discharged it. DONE when every id this feature owns carries a resolution
+line with its evidence in `.agent/live_review.md`, or is carried by name to the next paydown
+feature in this feature's closure. The soft limit is 8 sessions (amend0911-feedback rule B); at the
+limit the feature closes with what it resolved and carries the rest, which is not a split.
+
+## Why this exists
+Because the ledger only stays readable while it also shrinks. F284, the third paydown, read 4
+open findings at its claim and closed with the id below open; the `Owner:` line F284's closing
+round added to its paragraph in `.agent/live_review.md` moved it here, and DECISION F284 D3 gives
+the reason it was carried.
+
+## Carried from F284
+R-1008. It resolves only by a closure self-use run whose diff its reviewer passes, and F284's
+closure found no eligible self-use item.
+
+## Acceptance
+- R-1008 carries a resolution line naming a self-use run whose diff its reviewer passed, or is
+  carried by name to the next paydown feature at this closure.
+
+## Do not touch
+The resolutions F284 landed; the record is append-only.
+
+## Orchestrator brief
+At claim, the first round reads the open set with `open_finding_ids` of
+`scripts/rotate_live_review.py`, writes the slice list into this file and adds one Acceptance line
+for every other id it takes.
